The opportunity
Our hearing-care division makes the instruments clinicians use to test and fit patients. The R&amp;D group writes the software, electronics and test systems behind them, and we are now deciding how AI tools become part of that daily work.
&nbsp;
Coding assistants are moving fast, but in a regulated product every change still has to be reviewed and traced back to a requirement. You will design the AI-supported way of working together with our architect and developers, teach the teams to use it and keep improving it as it grows. You will report to the head of the digital engineering group.
&nbsp;
What you will do

Work hands-on with AI coding tools next to our developers and turn the patterns that work into shared templates and guidelines.
Build what is still missing: pipelines for AI-assisted changes, reusable agent parts, links to sources such as PLM, test management and regulatory records, access and data-location rules, and tracking of usage and cost.
Keep the architecture and module boundaries clean enough, with the architect, that agents can work inside them safely.
Agree with RA/QA how AI-assisted work meets IEC 62304 and our quality system.
Take the teams with you: pair, coach, demo and write it down until AI-assisted development is the normal way of working, not one expert's sid
